{
  "name": "lan-mouse",
  "description": "A high-performance software KVM switch implemented in Rust for seamless mouse and keyboard sharing across multiple local devices. It leverages platform-specific backends including Wayland (via libei and wlroots), X11, Windows, and macOS to capture and emulate input events. The system employs a custom UDP-based protocol for low-latency event streaming and a TCP layer for reliable state synchronization and configuration.",
